ventional fixed leg platforms and floating platforms attached to the sea floor with mooring lines, such as spars and tension leg platforms. This segment also provides management contract services to contracted rig platforms located in U.S. federal waters, the North Sea and Norwegian Sea off the coast of Norway, Caspian Sea, and other international waters. The Other Operations segment engages in manufacturing and engineering operations for the energy industry under the BENTEC name. Its technologies focus on developing, promoting, and commercializing technologies designed to enhance the drilling operations, as well as wellbore quality and placement. Helmerich & Payne, Inc. was founded in 1920 and is headquartered in Tulsa, Oklahoma.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Raymond John Adams III | CEO, President & Director | Age 39","culture_narrative":"Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["Helmerich & Payne, Inc. is a mid-cap energy business with a $3.2B market cap on $4.1B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +12% over the past three years and +10% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are contracting by -2.4pp, the first warning that competitive pressure is eroding the franchise.","Returns on capital run at 1% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $205M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 5 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 5.7\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin -4.4\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 3.2% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 3.8% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 89% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.8935600577813104},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.7) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Energy peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"red","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Operating margins softening -2.4pp YoY \u2014 early warning on the moat","sev":"amber","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Operating margins 26% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 9.3% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Geopolitical supply shocks \u2014 wars, sanctions, and OPEC decisions create volatility that no hedging programme can fully neutralise.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk","Energy sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 8% over 3 months"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"HP Q4 Earnings Beat Estimates on Higher U.S. Rig Activity","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3033199/hp-q4-earnings-beat-estimates-on-higher-u-s-rig-activity?cid=CS-ZC-FT-analyst_blog%7Cearnings_article-3033199","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795184580.0,"origin":"tiingo